        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T02:12:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this really sufficient to guarantee that the vaddr is backed by a `struct page`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5429,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 5429,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "0aca328104fd189ff78028672892ee8f63bcab30",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c9d4d62_cd02c0ff",
        "filename": "fs/f2fs/file.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1651802
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T22:16:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll build a bvec array from the vmap by walking it page by page and reject the dma_buf if any page is not backed by a valid struct page, instead of relying on vmalloc_to_page() inside the kvec iterator.",
      "parentUuid": "a2d00749_15257d7d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5429,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 5429,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "0aca328104fd189ff78028672892ee8f63bcab30",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6927f3e4_db1f39a1",
        "filename": "fs/f2fs/file.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1651802
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T03:38:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I kept the kvec instead of a bvec, since with a bvec the CPU writes (hole zeroing, buffered fallback) would go through the cacheable linear map, which breaks uncached dma_bufs. Before issuing each chunk, every page of the part read into the dma_buf is now checked with vmalloc_to_page()/virt_to_page() + pfn_valid(), the same lookup the block layer uses, and the ioctl returns -EOPNOTSUPP if any page fails.",
      "parentUuid": "6c9d4d62_cd02c0ff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5429,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 5429,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "0aca328104fd189ff78028672892ee8f63bcab30",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f344a48c_5a74cfb4",
        "filename": "fs/f2fs/file.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5466,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T02:12:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this ioctl be interruptible?  As-is, gigabytes can be read and the process will ignore SIGKILL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5466,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 5466,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "0aca328104fd189ff78028672892ee8f63bcab30",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf86ad70_33056a5c",
        "filename": "fs/f2fs/file.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5466,
      "author": {
        "id": 1651802
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T22:16:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed. I\u0027ll check fatal_signal_pending() before issuing each chunk, stop issuing and drain the in-flight chunks (at most depth x 4MB) before unmapping, and return -EINTR.",
      "parentUuid": "f344a48c_5a74cfb4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5466,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 5466,
        "endChar": 21
